## 2. Glossary

Original terms remain valid:

| Term | Definition |
|---|---|
| Session | A single logged period of study with a duration and timestamp. |
| XP | Experience points awarded for completed study time. |
| Medal | A daily award based on total study time for a calendar day. |
| Calendar Day | A local date from midnight to midnight, according to the user's system clock. |
| Day Attribution | The rule that determines which calendar day a session counts toward. |
| Streak | A count of consecutive qualifying study days. |
| Qualifying Day | A calendar day that counts toward a streak (≥10 minutes of study). |
| Active Day | A calendar day with at least one logged session. |
| Save File | The local JSON file containing user data and settings. |
| Backup File | A local copy of the last known good save file. |
| Frozen App | The application when packaged into a standalone executable. |
| Preset Session | A session logged using one of the predefined duration buttons. |
| Custom Session | A session logged using user-entered hours and minutes (or an auto-logged stopwatch run). |

Additional terms **[NEW]**:

| Term | Definition |
|---|---|
| Note | A user-created record with a title, free-text body, optional calendar-day attachment, and created/updated timestamps. |
| Dated note | A note attached to a specific calendar day; it also appears in that day's Calendar cell marker and Day Details dialog. |
| Undated note | A note with no day attachment (`day = None`); appears only in the Notes screen. |
| Stopwatch | The sidebar digital timer with Start/Stop/Reset that can auto-log a finished run as a study session. |
| Auto-log threshold | Minimum stopwatch run length (10 minutes) required for stopping to log a session. |
| Daily aggregate index | In-memory map of calendar day → (total minutes, total XP, medal, session ids), maintained incrementally by `AppState`. |
| Quarantine file | A copy of a corrupt/unreadable save or backup renamed with a `.corrupt` suffix and preserved for diagnosis. |
| AppState | The single in-memory coordinator between GUI screens, core engines, and the persistence repository. |
| ActionResult | Uniform `{ok, message, value}` result object returned by all state/actions operations to the GUI. |
| Performance gate | `scripts/perf_check.py`, which asserts timing budgets against a generated ~10,000-session dataset. |

