## 3. Confirmed Assumptions and Binding Decisions

All initial assumptions A-1 through A-13 remain binding and are implemented as stated (verified in `app/constants.py` and the core engines):

| ID | Decision | Consequence / Rule |
|---|---|---|
| A-1 | XP rate is **10 XP per completed 10 minutes**. | The default XP rate is fixed at 10 XP per completed 10-minute block (`XP_BLOCK_MINUTES = 10`, persisted setting `xp_per_10_minutes`). |
| A-2 | Partial 10-minute blocks award no XP. | Example: 25 minutes awards XP for 20 minutes only. |
| A-3 | Sessions that cross midnight are attributed entirely to the **calendar day on which they started**. | The full duration and XP count toward the start day. Sessions are not split across days. |
| A-4 | Custom session duration minimum is **5 minutes**, maximum is **12 hours**. | Sessions outside this range are rejected with a friendly validation message. |
| A-5 | Default save location is the current user's application data folder. | The save file is not required to be stored alongside the executable. See A-19 for the cross-platform resolution rule. |
| A-6 | "This week" means **Monday through Sunday**. | Statistics use a local calendar week starting on Monday (`week_bounds`). |
| A-7 | A streak counts a day only if the user studied for at least **10 minutes** on that day. | Days with less than 10 minutes do not extend or preserve a streak (`STREAK_QUALIFYING_MIN_MINUTES = 10`). |
| A-8 | v1 supports deleting sessions but not editing sessions. | Editing may be considered for a future version. Note editing exists and does not change this (see A-14). |
| A-9 | Manual "Load" replaces the current in-memory data after confirmation. | Loading a file is treated as replacing the current dataset (three-step flow, §6.5). |
| A-10 | Default theme is **dark mode**. | Dark mode is used on first run unless the user changes it (`DEFAULT_THEME = "dark"`). |
| A-11 | Medal counts in statistics use only the **highest medal earned per day**. | A 5-hour day counts as one Gold day, not Bronze, Silver, and Gold. |
| A-12 | Overlapping sessions are allowed and simply added together. | The application does not detect or prevent overlapping study entries. |
| A-13 | The app trusts the local system clock and does not synchronize time. | No network time, timezone correction, or server time validation is required. |

New/updated decisions **[NEW]/[UPDATED]**:

| ID | Decision | Consequence / Rule |
|---|---|---|
| A-14 | Notes are first-class persisted data alongside sessions. | Stored in the same JSON save file (`notes` array), covered by autosave, backup, atomic write, and recovery flows. Unlike sessions, notes **are** editable. |
| A-15 | Note limits are fixed: title ≤ 120 characters, body ≤ 100,000 characters. | Values are truncated defensively on load; a note with neither title nor body text is rejected with a friendly message. |
| A-16 | A stopwatch stop logs a session only when elapsed time ≥ 10 minutes (±0.25 s floating-point slack), rounded **down** to whole 10-minute steps. | Shorter stops preserve the reading so the run can be resumed; Reset always returns the display to zero without logging. Logged runs use the normal custom-session validation path. |
| A-17 | Stopwatch timing uses a monotonic clock, not wall-clock deltas. | Display accuracy survives delayed Tk callbacks; system clock changes do not distort a running measurement. |
| A-18 | Derived views are backed by an incrementally maintained daily index. | Adding/deleting a session updates only the affected day's aggregate; stats/calendar/home read the index. Deletion recomputes day XP from remaining sessions (partial-block rounding makes XP non-additive). |
| A-19 | Cross-platform data location *(updates A-5/A-13/NFR-1)*. | Default save directory resolves via `platformdirs.user_data_dir`: `%APPDATA%\StudyTrackerDesktop`-style per-user location on Windows and platform-standard locations on macOS/Linux. Windows remains the packaging/distribution target. |
| A-20 | Screens are constructed lazily on first visit. | Startup does not build the calendar grid, notes list, or stats cards until navigated to; unvisited screens are skipped by global refresh broadcasts. |

