## 4. Product Overview

Study Tracker Desktop is a personal productivity and gamification application. The user logs completed study sessions, receives XP for completed 10-minute blocks, and earns medals based on total study time per calendar day. The application provides:

- Quick study logging using preset durations (30 min / 1 h / 2 h) — one tap from Home.
- Custom study logging via a modal hours-and-minutes dialog with friendly inline validation (5 min – 12 h).
- **Study stopwatch [NEW]** in the sidebar with Start/Stop/Reset; stopping a run of ≥10 minutes auto-logs it as a custom session rounded down to the nearest 10 minutes.
- XP engine: 10 XP per completed 10-minute block (configurable/persisted rate, no UI editor in v1).
- Daily medals: Bronze ≥ 120 min, Silver ≥ 180 min, Gold ≥ 300 min (inclusive thresholds, highest medal only), shown as image badges with text fallback.
- Calendar view: Monday-first month grid with per-day medal icons and note-count markers, prev/next/today navigation, and a modal day-details dialog (totals, medal, session list with delete, attached notes with add/edit).
- **Notes [NEW]**: a full CRUD note-taking screen with search, list + detail panes, optional day attachment, and integration into Calendar and Day Details.
- Statistics: today/week/month/lifetime XP and time, current & longest streaks, total sessions, active days, average daily time, medal-day counts, and total-notes count.
- Settings: dark/light theme (persisted), manual Save, safe manual Load (validate → confirm → backup → replace), and data-status information (save path, session count, last saved, backup availability).
- Resilient local persistence: atomic JSON writes, single last-known-good backup, corrupt-file quarantine/recovery, schema-version protection, close-flush of unsaved changes.
- Standalone Windows executable (PyInstaller one-folder, windowed) with bundled assets; runnable from source on Windows/macOS/Linux.

The application shall **not** include: accounts/authentication, cloud synchronization, social features, telemetry, network connectivity requirements, multi-user profiles, or session editing.

