## 9. Error Handling and Edge Cases

Errors shall be handled in the style of a normal mobile app: friendly, non-technical, and recovery-oriented. ERR-1 … ERR-17 from the initial document are confirmed requirements, implemented as specified (friendly validation strings from `Session.validate_*`, confirmation dialogs, silent first-run creation, backup recovery with notice, quarantine preservation, partial-record skipping with the "some sessions could not be loaded" warning, future-schema refusal to overwrite, asset text fallbacks, disk-write errors keeping memory intact, clock/DST stability, friendly empty states, and exception-swallowing refresh guards):

| ID | Scenario | Required Behavior |
|---|---|---|
| ERR-1 | User enters a custom duration with non-numeric input. | Show a friendly validation message; do not log a session. |
| ERR-2 | User enters zero, negative, or otherwise invalid duration. | Show a friendly validation message; do not log a session. |
| ERR-3 | User enters a duration below 5 minutes or above 12 hours. | Show a friendly limit message; do not log a session. |
| ERR-4 | User enters minutes outside 0-59. | Show a friendly validation message. |
| ERR-5 | User attempts to delete a session. | Ask for confirmation before deletion. |
| ERR-6 | User attempts to load a file that would replace current data. | Ask for confirmation before proceeding. |
| ERR-7 | Save file is missing on first run. | Create a new empty data file with default settings; no error dialog is required. |
| ERR-8 | Save file is corrupt. | Attempt backup recovery. If backup fails, start with empty data and show a friendly warning. |
| ERR-9 | Backup file is corrupt. | Start with empty default data and show a friendly warning. Preserve corrupt files where practical. |
| ERR-10 | Save file contains a few invalid session records but is otherwise usable. | Skip or ignore invalid session records if possible, then notify the user that some data could not be loaded. |
| ERR-11 | Save file uses an unknown future schema version. | Do not overwrite the file. Show a friendly message that the file is from a newer version. |
| ERR-12 | Asset file is missing. | Use a text fallback or generic placeholder; do not crash. |
| ERR-13 | Disk write fails due to permissions or disk full. | Show a friendly error and keep the app usable in memory. Do not lose current in-memory data. |
| ERR-14 | System clock changes after sessions are logged. | Existing sessions remain attributed to their originally recorded start day. No retroactive rewriting. |
| ERR-15 | DST or timezone changes occur. | The application uses recorded local start dates and does not attempt to recompute historical sessions. |
| ERR-16 | User opens day details for a day with no sessions. | Show a friendly empty state. |
| ERR-17 | Unexpected internal error occurs. | Show a friendly error dialog, avoid crashing if possible, and preserve current data. |

Additional behaviours introduced with the new features **[NEW]**:

| ID | Scenario | Required Behavior |
|---|---|---|
| ERR-18 | Stopwatch auto-log fails validation unexpectedly. | Show the engine's friendly message; do not lose the elapsed display semantics defined in SW-5/SW-6. |
| ERR-19 | Note submitted with empty title and empty body. | Friendly rejection ("Give your note a title or some text before saving."); nothing stored. |
| ERR-20 | Note/day references point to a note id that no longer exists (stale UI). | Friendly "could not be found" message; no crash. |
| ERR-21 | Save payload contains duplicate session/note ids or malformed individual records. | Skip duplicates/invalid records, warn once with the partial-load message, load everything else. |
| ERR-22 | Note text fields arrive non-string or oversized in a hand-edited save file. | Coerce to string and clamp to limits (`sanitize_text`); never crash. |
| ERR-23 | Any screen's `refresh()` throws. | Exception is contained per-screen; other screens continue refreshing; app stays alive. |
| ERR-24 | Running without CustomTkinter installed from source. | `main.py` exits with a clear install-instruction message instead of a traceback. |

