|---|---|---|
| FUT-1 | Editing existing sessions. | Still out of scope (sessions: delete only). Note editing exists but does not change this. |
| FUT-2 | Study categories or subjects. | Still out of scope; Notes provide free-form context, not per-subject statistics. |
| FUT-3 | Real-time study timer. | **Delivered** as the sidebar Study Stopwatch (§6.8) — removed from the out-of-scope list. |
| FUT-4 | Reminders or notifications. | Still out of scope. |
| FUT-5 | Weekly goals. | Still out of scope (Home shows a next-medal progress bar, not user-defined goals). |
| FUT-6 | Achievements beyond daily medals. | Still out of scope. |
| FUT-7 | CSV export/import. | Still out of scope. |
| FUT-8 | Cloud backup or sync. | Still out of scope (explicitly offline). |
| FUT-9 | Multiple user profiles. | Still out of scope. |
| FUT-10 | Custom medal thresholds. | Still out of scope (fixed constants). |
| FUT-11 | Custom XP rates in the UI. | Still out of scope (rate persisted, no editor). |
| FUT-12 | Sound effects or animations. | Still out of scope. |
| FUT-13 | Minimize to tray. | Still out of scope. |
| FUT-14 | Portable mode alongside the executable. | Still out of scope (AppData/user-dir default). |

Candidate future ideas introduced by the new features (not requirements): note tagging/search ranking, stopwatch pause-vs-reset distinction surfacing, exporting notes, attaching notes to sessions, and a UI for editing the XP rate.
